      en: "The Lilongwe War Memorial, built in 1923, commemorates soldiers from Malawi (then Nyasaland) who died in World War I. It consists of a 12-meter-tall granite obelisk on a hill in central Lilongwe. Originally erected in Zomba, the monument was relocated to Lilongwe in 1975 after the capital moved. Names of the fallen are inscribed on its base. It is the site of annual Remembrance Day services, honoring both African and European soldiers. The memorial is a significant historical landmark, reflecting Malawi's involvement in global conflicts and its colonial past.",
